Reproduced from hart.h:49, 61, 73 and 85 (et-platform 836a4ab):
- get_shire_id = hart_id >> 6;
- get_neighborhood_id = (hart_id % 64) >> 4;
- get_minion_id = hart_id >> 1;
- get_thread_id = hart_id & 1.

In 'hartid = shire × 64 + minion × 2 + thread', minion runs 0-31 within the shire. But hartid >> 1 is shire × 32 + minion. Hart 130 is shire 2, in-shire minion 1, thread 0, yet 130 >> 1 = 65.

Only facts-arch.json:90 and build_facts_arch.py:89 carry the formula. The value 2048 and its N use are unaffected.

